    </div>
    <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Is this a PIM, or do we still need a separate one?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>It performs the role a PIM plays: a centralized product record holding catalog information, variants, images, enrichments, and digital assets, with catalog imports from external systems, scheduled publishing, and omnichannel synchronization to POS, e-commerce, marketplaces, and third-party channels. Because it is native to the platform your stores already run on, product data reaches the point of sale without a separate integration between a standalone PIM and your POS.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How does Teamwork Commerce manage product data?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Product information lives in one centralized record, catalog details, variants, images, enrichments, and digital assets. That record is the single source of truth read by POS, e-commerce, marketplaces, and any third-party channel, so the same product looks the same everywhere it appears.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Can product updates be scheduled ahead of a launch?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. You can stage the next version of a product alongside the live one and schedule publishing dates per market, down to the minute. The current version stays released until the scheduled moment, so seasonal changes and drops go live exactly when planned without anyone touching the live record.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          What does AI do for product content?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>AI generates product descriptions, translations, search terms, imagery, and video from the record you already have, working within a library of brand messaging so output stays on-brand. It also powers conversational product search for associates and personalized product recommendations they can share with a customer.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How does product data reach the point of sale?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Omnichannel catalog synchronization keeps product information consistent across POS, e-commerce, marketplaces, and third-party channels, so the same description, variant, and imagery appear everywhere. Existing catalog data imports from external systems, and publishing dates control when updates become available.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
